Recommendation
Implement centralized exception handling for all unhandled exceptions.
Display only a generic error message to end users (e.g., "An unexpected error occurred. Please contact support.").
Log detailed exception information only to secure server-side or application logs.
Remove stack traces, source code paths, namespaces, method names, and line numbers from user-facing error messages.
Build production releases without debug information.
Ensure detailed diagnostic information is accessible only to authorized administrators or developers.
